{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-110617-r4510170","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Lemon Rosemary Pork Tenderloin","sourcePageId":110617,"sourceRevision":"4510170","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-16T02:01:36Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Lemon%20Rosemary%20Pork%20Tenderloin&oldid=4510170","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:14.377Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using canola oil","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using lemon zest","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using rosemary","Category:Roasted recipes","Category:Southern U.S. recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1d79c6aa6e9fe7a4950bbd963600eafee9b81d17222ce052042cb03a2221aa9a","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Pork recipes|servings=8 servings|time=About an hour|difficulty=1\n}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Southern cuisine|Southern U.S. Cooking]] | [[Cookbook:Meat|Meats]]\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chop|finely chopped]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive]] or [[Cookbook:Canola Oil|canola oil]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Rosemary|fresh rosemary]]\n* 1 teaspoon minced [[Cookbook:Thyme|fresh thyme]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Grating|grated]] [[Cookbook:Lemon Rind|lemon peel]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic clove]], minced\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. (2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] / 900 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] tenderloins\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Combine the chopped onion, oil, lemon juice, rosemary, thyme, lemon peel, minced garlic, salt, and pepper. Rub this mixture over tenderloins.\n# Let the tenderloins [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]], refrigerated, for as long as you want, or just immediately proceed with cooking.\n# Place the meat on a rack in a shallow roasting pan.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] uncovered at [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|400°F]] (205°C) or until a meat [[Cookbook:Thermometer|thermometer]] reads 160°F (70°C).\n# Cover with [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]] and let stand 10 minutes before slicing.\n\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rosemary]]\n[[Category:Roasted recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon zest]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Lemon Rosemary Pork Tenderloin","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 medium onion, finely chopped","sourceText":"1 medium onion, finely chopped","amountText":"1 medium onion, finely chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tablespoon olive or canola oil","sourceText":"2 tablespoon olive or canola oil","amountText":"2 tablespoon olive or canola oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id"